  {
    "episode_id": 73193,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/3/73193.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 16,
    "turn_text": "And the Chinese take on the prior advantage. They subsidize their corporations. They give a wink and a nod, call them private companies. They're not. And they don't have to comply with any of the restrictions that our companies have to comply with. So these tariffs actually level the playing field. And many, many conservatives have taken issue with Trump over this. But my feeling is that we have been so unfairly positioned by presidents of the past, both Democrats and Republicans, that President Trump understands as a business guy that if we're going to create jobs, we have to level that blank field and this is one way to do it. Now another way he's been doing that is his recent decision on Mexico. He made big news last week when he came out and said he's going to level a tariff on Mexico if they did not start stealing off their border. and refusing to allow these care rounds of tens of thousands of people to pass through Mexico and just enter the U.S., the U.S. borders being overwhelmed. We've talked about that on many shows, but over the weekend, Mexico sent its top negotiator and they cut a deal. Not Democrats are furious over it. Beto Rorick, I consider him a friend. He's a Democrat out of El Paso, and I don't agree on any issues, but we worked in Congress together.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
