    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/3/73193.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 33,
    "turn_text": "Many people did not know that the sale of body parts was actually occurring here in the Mexico as well as across the country. And so Trump, again, was derided by conservatives that never trumpers in the Republican Party. He said he's not conservative, and they had never, never, never supported him. He's doing more conservative things, actually, than any president before, or I suspect it'll be a long time before we see another president that is this active. He said that he just didn't understand the life issue. He never thought much about it, and the women's right to choose. He just kind of brushed it aside. But when he got to understanding the issue, then he's come out and and been a very pro-life president. And so last week he canceled a $2 million federal contract which purchased body parts from reported babies and then used them in research. And so the National Institutes for Health and the federal drug administration had the federal contract with the University of California in San Francisco. And they were using body parts from babies that were 18 to 24 weeks of age for supposed to research. In New Mexico, the same thing was going on with the University of New Mexico. And of course, at some point, the pressure on the institution became so strong that they canceled that research and actually laid off the person that was involved in it. One more indication that the nation is really waking up to the conservative viewpoints So in the last segment we talked about having democratic supporters complaining about the increase in minimum wage here You have obviously 70 to 75% of Americans including Democrats and independents as well as Republicans who are saying late term abortions should not be occurring And when they find that the tissue from those babies was being used in research, then they objected to that. And so we just defined that the nation is beginning to recall at some of the radical policies of the left. And of course, our own governor way over reached in this last legislative cycle. in the 60-day session January, February, and March, and tried to pass the most radical late-term abortion bill in the nation, and was turned down when six or eight Democrats in the Senate joined with Republicans to defeat that measure. And now they're being targeted by their own party, the progressives, and their party are targeting those conservative Democrats. And so I always tell my friends, be sure and go out say a word of gratitude to the people who will stand on principle. You can find that list of senators on our webpage and take a look at it but big news happening from Trump but nationwide in the life issue.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
