    "turn_text": "You recall last March 15th is when that shooter came out and New Zealand and murdered innocent people. And I think it was the shooter himself that said that now the laws are going to change. And New Zealand, and sure enough, they did. Well, that was not the last word. Everybody assumed it was that the last week then was the first day that citizens were supposed to turn over their handguns, only 530 out of 300,000 people's long guns actually turned them in. And so the population is beginning to stand up, even when the government takes sides on issues and says that they're going to do one thing, like you're saying, here in the Mexico The sheriff stood up and told the state legislature and the governor that we're not going to enforce your laws on these gun bans. And so the population, the citizens are standing up, fighting around them that glow. And it's really good to see because our family fathers started this country, a government out of the people, violent people, a court of people with the idea that kings and strong central governments are never good for people. and around the globe now it's being affirmed in one measure after another. So seeing the way that that is played out in New Zealand, seeing the way that it's played out in New Mexico, we as human beings all share the same sort of makeup, the same sort of desirable freedom, liberty and",
